  "summary": "Four documents directly apply gradient boosted tree ensembles to battery remaining life estimation, and one additional document applies the method to a different topic (protein molecular function) and is included only to complete five candidates. The core relevant studies are: [V0085] Gupta et al. (2024), which applies boosted decision-tree ensembles to the CellLife dataset and reports accuracy of 0.74; [V0086] Haddad et al. (2025), which evaluates boosted decision-tree ensembles on ToxiBench and reports MAE of 0.81; [V0088] Brennan et al. (2018), which applies boosted decision-tree ensembles to the ProtMap dataset and reports F1 of 0.60; and [V0087] Adebayo et al. (2026), which applies boosted decision-tree ensembles to the GridWatch dataset and reports AUROC of 0.88. Documents that only mention boosted decision-tree ensembles for battery remaining life as prior work (e.g., V0214, V0152, V0054, V0198, V0197) are excluded as they do not constitute direct applications. [V0160] El-Sayed et al. (2021) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles but to protein molecular function on MetroFlow (AUROC 0.76), making it only marginally relevant as a fifth-ranked entry.",
